    wowFact: 'Feynman, Schwinger and Tomonaga shared the 1965 Nobel Prize. Their approaches could hardly have been more different: Feynman used intuitive graphical "Feynman diagrams"; Schwinger wielded dense, formal operator mathematics; Tomonaga had independently developed the method during wartime in Japan with limited access to Western physics journals.',
