    detail: "Bell\'s theorem is one of the most profound results in all of physics. It transformed Einstein\'s 1935 EPR thought experiment from a philosophical debate into a precise, testable prediction. Bell proved that any theory using local hidden variables — where particles carry pre-determined properties and influence cannot travel faster than light — must obey certain statistical inequalities (Bell inequalities) in the correlations between measurements. Quantum mechanics predicts these inequalities will be violated. The theorem therefore provided a clean experimental test: measure the correlations between entangled particles and check whether they exceed the classical Bell bound. If they do, hidden variables are ruled out and quantum entanglement is real. Alain Aspect\'s 1982 experiments, and increasingly rigorous tests since, have confirmed Bell inequality violations with extraordinary precision.",
